WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.507 --> 00:00:06.061
For Groomer Books, two boxes are filled, three wait, and every job has one owner.

2
00:00:06.081 --> 00:00:08.038
Here's the example chart.

3
00:00:08.058 --> 00:00:12.989
The founder sits at the top and approves anything external or about money.

4
00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:17.414
The finance assistant is Claude Pro with a Groomer Books project.

5
00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:22.264
It sorts receipts and drafts overdue-invoice reminders each Monday.

6
00:00:22.284 --> 00:00:29.274
It reads the invoicing app as a viewer, and drafts in Gmail, never sending without a yes.

7
00:00:29.294 --> 00:00:32.761
Product and website is free GitHub plus Claude Pro.

8
00:00:32.781 --> 00:00:37.523
The chief of staff will be Claude Duet once the waitlist lets the account in.

9
00:00:37.543 --> 00:00:40.352
Until then, that box says open.

10
00:00:40.416 --> 00:00:44.752
Sales and customers, and marketing and content, say me for now.

11
00:00:44.772 --> 00:00:53.882
The audit found two fixes: remove calendar access the finance assistant didn't need, and add delete to the chief of staff's rule.

12
00:00:53.902 --> 00:01:00.352
The next hire is marketing and content, for the Instagram posts, forty-five minutes a week.

13
00:01:00.372 --> 00:01:03.124
And the Friday review is on the calendar.

